What is Rubber Tracks?
Rubber tracks are flexible, high‑traction alternatives to conventional steel tracks used on equipment across construction, agriculture, forestry and mining sectors. They consist of layered reinforced rubber combined with high‑tensile steel or fiber cords and advanced elastomers. This architecture delivers strong traction while substantially lowering ground pressure, reducing surface damage on soft or environmentally‑sensitive terrains, and providing smoother ride quality for operators.
